{"id": "20551451", "revid": "45417033", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20551451", "title": "Warren White House", "text": "The Warren White House is a historic house in Waltham, Massachusetts. The -story wood-frame house was built c. 1850\u201354, and is the oldest surviving house on Warren Street, once an important thoroughfare between Waltham and Belmont. The house has classic Italianate styling, with a symmetrical three-bay facade, wide cornerboards and entablature, and round-arched gable windows. It was built by Warren White, a wheelwright, on land owned by David White, a farmer, who sold Warren White the property in 1855.\nThe house was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1989."}
