{"id": "20552603", "revid": "41210608", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20552603", "title": "Carl Bennett", "text": "Carl Blair Bennett (December 7, 1915 \u2013 May 15, 2013) was an American professional basketball general manager and head coach. He was born in Rockford, Indiana and began his sports career by playing softball. Bennett was recruited by Fred Zollner in 1938 to join his staff. He coached the Fort Wayne Zollner Pistons of the National Basketball League (NBL) and then the Fort Wayne Pistons of the Basketball Association of America (BAA). for six games in 1948\u201349. Bennett became the franchise's general manager and served in that capacity from 1948 to 1954. Bennett endured a 15-year campaign to get Zollner inducted into the Naismith Memorial Basketball Hall of Fame, which occurred in 1999. Bennett died at the age of 97 in 2013.\nHead coaching record.\nSource"}
